SUMMARY:NC Arboretum Blue Ghost Firefly Night Hike
DESCRIPTION:NC Arboretum Blue Ghost Firefly Night Hike\nwith Shane Myers and Asheville Wellness Tours \nWednesday\, May 13  |  7:30 – 10:30 pm \n(rain date is Thursday\, May 14) \nREGISTER HERE \nImmerse yourself in the magic of twilight and experience the wonders of nighttime in the Blue Ridge Mountains. From sunset and starry skies to fireflies\, we’ll marvel at Mother Nature’s light shows as we explore the forest\, hoping to encounter the elusive Blue Ghost Firefly species! Out of the 26 species of firefly we have in western North Carolina\, the Blue Ghost (Phausis reticulata) might be the most magical. With a very limited range\, and a distinctive meandering flight\, we have a lot to learn from observing these nocturnal jewels. Tonight we’ll talk about what makes a firefly light up\, what their lives are like\, and how we can make sure they are around for generations to come. \nShane Myers’ interest in nature began as a child with a love of dinosaurs. This quickly grew to include fossils\, insects\, and reptiles\, and learning from the notes his grandparents kept of the birds that came to their feeders in Toledo\, Ohio. He has a Bachelors of Science in Wildlife Biology and did most of his undergraduate work on dragonflies and damselflies. He’s assisted in outreach and education for plant conservation groups\, Odonata Groups\, and various bird groups. Shane currently works for the Adult Education department at the NC Arboretum. \nThis event is a collaboration with Asheville Wellness Tours and they are handling all of the registration through their system. They have graciously included our Membership Discount promo code in their system so if you are an Arboretum member don’t forget to input your code to get your 10% off. Registration proceeds will be shared by both the North Carolina Arboretum and Asheville Wellness Tours. \nThis program takes place off-site near Mills River and more details will be given out to registrants as the date gets closer. This program will take place outside and will follow easy trails and paved walkways. Dress for the weather and prepare to be outside for the entire program time. \n\nMembers: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions. \nSee a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs.\nFollow us on Facebook & Instagram!\nJoin our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord!\nInterested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here.\n\nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/blue_ghost_awt/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/AshevilleWellnessTours-Blue-Ghost-Tours-Fireflies-03.jpg
END:VEVENT
